# AnchorPoint Mesh — anchorpoint   # Render: scripts/render-diagrams.sh deployments/mesh/architecture.d2

title: |md
  # AnchorPoint · 2-site link
point-to-point WireGuard link · overlay 10.0.80.0/24 · every node is also an exit
| {near: top-center}

hamburg: Hamburg · DE {
  style.fill: "#d6e4ff"
  id: "HAMBURG  (10.0.80.1)"
  local: "local: AnchorPoint-HAM\n192.168.10.0/24 · ether3/ether4/ether5"
  exits: "exit via 1 peer(s)\nether2 + Wi-Fi"
  clients: "test clients: iphone, macbook\nwg-clients 10.0.91.0/24 · UDP 51823"
}
barcelona: Barcelona · ES {
  style.fill: "#d6f5d6"
  id: "BARCELONA  (10.0.80.2)"
  local: "local: AnchorPoint-BCN\n192.168.20.0/24 · ether3/ether4/ether5"
  exits: "exit via 1 peer(s)\nether2 + Wi-Fi"
  clients: "test clients: iphone, macbook\nwg-clients 10.0.92.0/24 · UDP 51823"
}

# One WireGuard tunnel per unordered pair (dedupe: this.index < remote.index)
hamburg <-> barcelona: "UDP 51820" {style.stroke-dash: 3}

note: |md
  Each edge is a WireGuard tunnel on its own UDP port (both ends forward it).
  Plug into a node's exit port / join its exit SSID to browse from that country.
  Each site also serves roaming test clients (iPhone + MacBook) on wg-clients.
| {near: bottom-center}
